!!id:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/temporal.tn?sha256=e839a87b7e98ca1185a4a9fb2f364e770603a0f4f60cc4b4e26faa4cc02759b8"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/meta.tn?sha256=fba10509f9c9db688ee01d2921635a24b1879d80b19f43c59edba3674c18252d"
@doc:"""
  The TSON temporal library: `date`, `time`, `datetime`, `duration` and
  `period`, each RFC 3339's. A schema imports it, or core.tn, to write them
  ([TSON-DATA] §5.4, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.5). numeric.tn's shared rules for bounds
  and `multiple_of` apply.
  """
!schema {
  @doc:"""
    The temporal constructors, each named by its path, `temporal.date_type`.
    """
  temporal => !schema {
    @doc:"""
      The constructor of `date`: RFC 3339 `full-date`. An author refines the
      instance: `recent => !date ^ { min: 2000-01-01 }`.
      """
    date_type => meta.atom & atom.specification & {
      spec?: = "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339"
      ( min: date | exclusive_min: date )?
      ( max: date | exclusive_max: date )?
    }

    @doc:"""
      The constructor of `time`: RFC 3339 `full-time`. The value is the time of
      day in UTC, on [00:00:00, 24:00:00): the offset is a spelling, so
      `10:00:00+01:00` and `09:00:00Z` are one value, and `23:30:00-02:00` is
      `01:30:00Z`. A leap second, `23:59:60`, is refused.

      `precision: N` admits a value that is a whole number of 10^-N seconds, N
      at most 9. It constrains the value and not a spelling: `12:00:00.500` is
      admitted under `precision: 1`, and is written `12:00:00.5`.
      """
    time_type => meta.atom & atom.specification & {
      spec?:      = "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339"
      ( min: time | exclusive_min: time )?
      ( max: time | exclusive_max: time )?
      precision?: numeric.count
    }

    @doc:"""
      The constructor of `datetime`: RFC 3339 `date-time`. The value is the
      instant on the UTC timeline: the offset is a spelling, so
      `2026-01-01T10:00:00+01:00` and `2026-01-01T09:00:00Z` are one value, and
      `-00:00` is the same instant as `Z`. A leap second is refused. `precision`
      is `time_type`'s.
      """
    datetime_type => meta.atom & atom.specification & {
      spec?:      = "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339"
      ( min: datetime | exclusive_min: datetime )?
      ( max: datetime | exclusive_max: datetime )?
      precision?: numeric.count
    }

    @doc:"""
      The constructor of `duration`. The value is a signed exact decimal number
      of seconds: `PT90M`, `PT1H30M` and `P0DT5400S` are one value, and so are
      `PT0S`, `P0D` and `-PT0S`. A day is 86400 s and a week 7 days.

      The lexical form is RFC 3339 Appendix A's `duration` with an optional
      leading `-`; a fraction on the seconds component only, written with `.`
      (`PT0.5S`, never `PT1.5H`); any of D, H, M, S omitted, at least one
      present and in order; and no Y or month-M component (`P1M` is a `period`,
      a minute `PT1M`). `PnW` stands alone (`P1W2D` is an error).

      The seconds component has at most nine fractional digits, and a magnitude
      does not exceed 2^63 - 1 nanoseconds. A processor MUST represent every
      value in that range and MUST reject one outside it whether or not its own
      representation could hold it.

      `precision` is `time_type`'s. `multiple_of` is a step over the seconds
      count: `PT15M` admits only quarter-hour values.
      """
    duration_type => meta.atom & atom.specification & {
      spec?:       = "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339#appendix-A"
      ( min: duration | exclusive_min: duration )?
      ( max: duration | exclusive_max: duration )?
      precision?:  numeric.count
      multiple_of?: duration
    }

    @doc:"""
      The constructor of `period`. The value is a signed integer number of
      months: `P1Y` and `P12M` are one value, and so are `P0Y`, `P0M` and
      `-P0M`. The lexical form is RFC 3339 Appendix A's `duration` restricted to
      an optional leading `-`, then `P` with a Y component, an M component, or
      both in that order: no fraction, no W or D component and no `T` part.
      """
    period_type => meta.atom & atom.specification & {
      spec?:       = "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339#appendix-A"
      ( min: period | exclusive_min: period )?
      ( max: period | exclusive_max: period )?
      multiple_of?: period
    }
  }

  @doc:"A calendar date, `2026-01-31`."
  @atom.ordering:TOTAL @atom.bounded:true
  date => !temporal.date_type {}

  @doc:"""
    A time of day with a mandatory offset. Two spellings of one UTC time are one
    value.
    """
  @atom.ordering:TOTAL @atom.bounded:true
  time => !temporal.time_type {}

  @doc:"""
    A date and time with a mandatory offset: an instant, so two spellings of one
    instant are one value.
    """
  @atom.ordering:TOTAL @atom.bounded:true
  datetime => !temporal.datetime_type {}

  @doc:"""
    Elapsed time as an exact number of seconds, `PT1H30M`. It has no year or
    month component: a calendar span is a `period`.
    """
  @atom.ordering:TOTAL @atom.bounded:true
  duration => !temporal.duration_type {}

  @doc:"A calendar span as a whole number of months, `P1Y6M`."
  @atom.ordering:TOTAL @atom.bounded:false
  period => !temporal.period_type {}
}